# Slab staging: bottom vs top-half (rotation bit 2) slabs, a
# bottom-over-top pair reading as a full block, and a top slab hanging
# under a full block. Flat floor is SANDSTONE at y=0; AIR starts at y=1.
wait_idle 20 6000
# Bottom slabs: the plain placement shape sits in the cell's lower half.
setblock 10 1 8 OAK_SLAB
setblock 11 1 8 STONE_SLAB
# Top-half slabs (BLOCK_ROTATE_SLAB_TOP = rotation bit 2 = 4).
setblock 10 1 10 OAK_SLAB 4
setblock 11 1 10 STONE_SLAB 4
# A top slab under a bottom slab: the pair reads as a solid block.
setblock 14 1 10 OAK_SLAB 4
setblock 14 2 10 OAK_SLAB
# A top slab hanging under a full block: its underside shows mid-cell and
# its top face is culled against the block above.
setblock 17 3 10 STONE
setblock 17 2 10 STONE_SLAB 4
wait 30
assert_block 10 1 8 OAK_SLAB
assert_block 10 1 10 OAK_SLAB
assert_block 14 1 10 OAK_SLAB
assert_block 14 2 10 OAK_SLAB
assert_block 17 2 10 STONE_SLAB
# Face-on view of the two rows: bottom row sits low in-cell, top row high.
camera 12 3.5 5 180 20
wait 20
screenshot halves
# The paired column at x=14 reads as a continuous block face.
camera 14 3.5 7 180 20
wait 20
screenshot paired
# Looking up at the hanging slab under the stone block.
camera 17 2.3 13.5 180 -15
wait 20
screenshot hanging
# Underside lighting: floating bottom slabs (left) and top slabs (right)
# at the same z — both undersides should read the same mid-gray.
setblock 9 3 13 OAK_SLAB
setblock 10 3 13 OAK_SLAB
setblock 11 3 13 OAK_SLAB
setblock 13 3 13 OAK_SLAB 4
setblock 14 3 13 OAK_SLAB 4
setblock 15 3 13 OAK_SLAB 4
wait 30
camera 12 1.5 8.5 180 -35
wait 20
screenshot undersides
echo slabs done
